WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.480
Things are just heated
between the two of you.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.960
They're not heated.

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.800
They've cooled down.

4
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.640
I'll go and talk to him.

5
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.680
About what?
That I'm really cute and sweet?

6
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.560
No.

7
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.440
Laura.

8
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.120
Can I stay the night?

9
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.440
God.

10
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.040
Please? Just for one night.

11
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.040
We'll do yoga in the morning.

12
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.040
I just need to take some time off.

13
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.560
Alright, of course you can stay.
You can stay in my room.

14
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.080
Good God,
I don't want to talk to him.

15
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.720
I'll talk to him myself.
You stay here.

16
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.880
Did she come here?
- Yes, she's here.

17
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.960
No-no, don't go!

18
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.040
I don't understand.
Did she move in with you?

19
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.680
Yes. No.

20
00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.240
It's a ladies' thing.
Laura's talking to her.

21
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.920
I think she wants to be alone
or think about things.

22
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:03.960
I don't understand.

23
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.240
Calm down.
Let's go to yours.

24
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.000
DIVORCE IN PEACE

25
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.240
Should I continue?

26
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.480
We've made it to the last card.

27
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.160
Aksel, put that away.

28
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.040
We don't have to do these
tasks at home. I can't force you.

29
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.080
Let's just listen.

30
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.480
I messed up because of you.

31
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.520
Our time is almost over.

32
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.160
Please, just listen until the end.
- Alright.

33
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.840
It doesn't matter.
Let's finish this abracadabra.

34
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.240
So...

35
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.880
The last step towards
a happy divorce.

36
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:52.400
It's a logical last step
for this journey.

37
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.840
You will write a farewell letter
to each other.

38
00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.000
Of course.

39
00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.120
That's a beautiful idea.

40
00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.360
You'll write your letters
and then read them to each other.

41
00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.680
In a warm and sweet setting.

42
00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.040
Meditative?

43
00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.200
Exactly.

44
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.440
And then that's it.

45
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.960
Then, you're ready.

46
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.720
A farewell letter.

47
00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.880
My letter will be short and concrete.

48
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.080
Make yourself comfortable here.

49
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.720
Honestly, I'm so embarrassed.

50
00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.840
What for?

51
00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.720
Where will you sleep?

52
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.640
I think we can manage
in the living room.

53
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.680
The sheets are clean
and everything's fine.

54
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.720
It doesn't make sense.

55
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.840
I don't understand anymore.

56
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.640
First, I'm too jealous,

57
00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.280
then I'm not jealous enough.

58
00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.880
Jealous and jealous.

59
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.440
I'm walking on a thread
all the time.

60
00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.760
Tiptoe on the thinnest
piece of thread for a woman.

61
00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.720
Mirjam's stressed.

62
00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.240
She'll calm down by the morning.

63
00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.920
Everything was perfect.

64
00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:35.760
Everything was fine,
things were going well and now?

65
00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.120
Laura will talk to her.
- Laura.

66
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.480
You know what I think?

67
00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:44.160
Mirjam thinks that you're not
paying enough attention to her.

68
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.240
What?

69
00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.160
Tauno, calm down.
Remember what we had.

70
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.600
Tauno's five step therapy plan
for staying together.

71
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.080
Yes, but I've been using it
the entire time.

72
00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.680
Damn it,
I take care of Mirjam like...

73
00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.440
I take care of her...
Damn it, I cherish her!

74
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.960
I've been throwing money at her.

75
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.400
She doesn't know the real world.
Let her leave!

76
00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.280
Let her live somewhere else
for two days

77
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.320
and then she'll realise what
she'll be giving up if she leaves.

78
00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.560
Tauno, calm down.

79
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.480
In the morning, you two will sit down
and have a nice calm chat.

80
00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.400
Do some yoga together.
Clear things up.

81
00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.920
Yoga? Yeah, right.
I have my own therapy.

82
00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.120
Psychotherapy for the Estonian man.

83
00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.920
Listen to this.
This is what I'll do.

84
00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.480
This is what I'll do.

85
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.040
I'm going to have a sauna.

86
00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.560
I'll heat the sauna up to 120° C,

87
00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.040
grab a crate of beer
and lock the door from the inside.

88
00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:45.440
In the morning, I'll be new and clean
both from the inside and outside.

89
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.160
Let's go.

90
00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.640
A crate of beer and 120° C.

91
00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.480
Do you remember that summer

92
00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.560
when we had to sleep
on the floor at my parents'?

93
00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.920
Right before we got our flat.

94
00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.760
Yeah, I do.

95
00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.760
My dad was all ears.

96
00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.600
We had to be so quiet
because the walls were so thin.

97
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.760
Your dad was a sleepwalker.

98
00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.520
He kept stumbling around
the apartment.

99
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.680
We kept sneaking glances
from under the covers.

100
00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.480
We didn't dare to breathe
while we were making Ave.

101
00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.560
Good night, honey.

102
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.040
Good night, honey.

103
00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.640
You look very good.
Very chic.

104
00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:01.920
Do I look proper?
- Yes.

105
00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.360
Stop. One thing.

106
00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.600
We'll take this off.

107
00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.720
That bouquet looks nice.
Did you choose it yourself?

108
00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.440
Yeah.
What a circus.

109
00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.600
Listen, I'm sorry.
- Don't worry about it.

110
00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:15.920
Come on, give us a twirl.
- Quality control?

111
00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:19.840
Not bad.

112
00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:23.040
Very nice. Go upstairs.

113
00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:25.000
She's still asleep.
- Asleep?

114
00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.480
Go wake her up.

115
00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.880
If anything, give us a call.

116
00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.480
You can come for a consultation
where we can talk things through.

117
00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.200
The main thing is

118
00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:54.280
to take everything playfully.

119
00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.760
Thank you.
Really, thanks a lot.

120
00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.760
When you've finished
all the therapy tasks,

121
00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.520
come back here
and let me know how it went.

122
00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.600
We'll definitely come.

123
00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.400
It's included in the price.
- That's great. Aksel?

124
00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.840
Thanks for helping
with the demolition. Let's go.

125
00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.240
No problem.
Therapy is meant to help.

126
00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.640
What are they doing there?
- I don't know. They went silent.

127
00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.800
Is that a good or a bad thing?
- I don't know.

128
00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.640
Mom. Dad.
- Shush.

129
00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.320
Tauno and Mirjam are reconciling.

130
00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.440
Are they fighting now?

131
00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:41.320
No, they're not fighting.
They're just reconciling.

132
00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.640
I have that exam today.

133
00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.920
Wish me luck.
- That's nice, good luck.

134
00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.160
I'll take it down after.
- Yeah, yeah.

135
00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.600
Yeah.

136
00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.480
Easy, easy, easy.

137
00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:07.840
We decided to try again.

138
00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.360
Thank God.

139
00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.040
That's a wonderful decision.

140
00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.800
Thank you.

141
00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.840
Sorry for the choice of day, Laura.

142
00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.200
What day?

143
00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.560
We're taking the divorce papers
to the vital statistics office today.

144
00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:23.760
Shit...

145
00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.240
It's official?

146
00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.600
You're going on that
date with Rihard tonight?

147
00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.480
Okay...

148
00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:36.600
Wait.

149
00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.560
Do we have the divorce papers?

150
00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.760
We have everything.

151
00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:44.640
We have to pay the state fee.

152
00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.480
The state fee?
- Yeah.

153
00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:49.000
50 euros.
- Damn.

154
00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.840
Marriage costs 30 euros.

155
00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.880
Divorce is an expensive pleasure.

156
00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.720
Marriage is cheaper.

157
00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:57.960
Yeah.

158
00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.440
If everyone in Estonia got a divorce,

159
00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:03.640
we could finally build
that bridge to Saaremaa.

160
00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.680
But if everyone got married,
we wouldn't be able to do that.

161
00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.080
We'd get half way.

162
00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.320
We'd get a springboard
instead of a bridge.

163
00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:14.640
Jump to Saaremaa.

164
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.520
Do we have to pay in cash?
I think I have...

165
00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.040
Don't.
- Want to split it?

166
00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.520
I'll pay it myself.
I can pay by card.

167
00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:25.760
Seriously?

168
00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.840
Such a modern thing.
E-government.

169
00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.760
Swipe to divorce.

170
00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.960
I don't know.

171
00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:38.520
Do we go in?

172
00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:41.560
Well...

173
00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:43.520
Let's go.

174
00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.520
Don't forget, you have to
write me that farewell letter.

175
00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.280
Yeah, and you to me.
- Yes.

176
00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.560
I've already started
reading Shakespeare.

177
00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.240
To improve my style.
- You don't say.

178
00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.560
Yeah.

179
00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.720
Another surprise.

180
00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.080
Well?

181
00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.440
How did the exam go?

182
00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.800
Pretty well.
The feedback was positive.

183
00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:21.600
Don't know the results yet.

184
00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.160
Okay.

185
00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:24.920
Today's the day?

186
00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.960
Today is the official day?

187
00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.200
Yeah.

188
00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:35.920
What do we do?

189
00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.560
I was thinking...

190
00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:41.840
We should set the table for them.

191
00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.800
Weird.

192
00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:48.200
I was in mom's stomach
during the wedding.

193
00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.240
And now I can arrange
their divorce party.

194
00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.720
Alma really is...
- Yeah, she is.

195
00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.080
She does look like mom.

196
00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:19.840
So...

197
00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.200
Thank you.

198
00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:24.600
And thank you.

199
00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.360
An official thank you.

200
00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.320
Thank you.

201
00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.680
It was a good ride.

202
00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:39.200
Just over 25 years.

203
00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.600
We had some unexpected
twists before the finish too.

204
00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.840
Yeah.

205
00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:49.840
Well...

206
00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.880
Do you need help finding a rental?
- No, I've already found one.

207
00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:56.760
I'm checking it out tomorrow.

208
00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.920
A new job as well.
- Really?

209
00:11:58.960 --> 00:11:59.960
Yeah.

210
00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.200
You've started taking action.

211
00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.560
Did I have any other choice?

212
00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.320
Where are you applying?

213
00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:09.280
A film score needs to be made.

214
00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.560
It's in a studio,
so no stage fright.

215
00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:14.520
Super.

216
00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.480
I guess it's a bye then.

217
00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:25.040
Look at this.
- God, this is beautiful.

218
00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:31.360
At least we made good children.

219
00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.840
I guess we can exchange
our farewell letters.

220
00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.000
Yeah.

221
00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.960
Here.
- Thanks.

222
00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.400
And then you can go on that date.

223
00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:52.920
With Rihard.

224
00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.000
No, I have time.

225
00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.200
You have time?

226
00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.200
Alright, then.

227
00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:06.280
Then we can do it in a
calm and meditative way.

228
00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.120
You've really changed.

229
00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.120
It's like you've woken up.

230
00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:25.040
If we didn't have this burden,
this marriage,

231
00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:28.760
if I looked at you with fresh eyes...
- We don't have any burdens.

232
00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.440
Indeed.

233
00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.720
We threw it away.

234
00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.520
Gave our signatures.

235
00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.680
Paid 50 euros.
- Yeah.

236
00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.800
Now we're just Aksel and Laura.

237
00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:46.760
Two Estonians.

238
00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:50.000
Cheers to Aksel and Laura.

239
00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:58.400
Now you can calmly talk about
you and Rihard.

240
00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:01.040
Calmly?

241
00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.960
Yeah, the date.

242
00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.520
It's a business dinner.

243
00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.200
We're selling our bakery
to his restaurant chain.

244
00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.520
That's it?

245
00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:11.440
Well...

246
00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.320
You can be honest.

247
00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:18.840
I promise I won't intervene.

248
00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:23.440
I'm politely giving you away.

249
00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.680
Only...

250
00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:27.720
What?

251
00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:30.680
It's hard for me.

252
00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:40.320
Rihard does expect
something from tonight.

253
00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.160
He's been giving some hints.

254
00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:44.280
What about you?

255
00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.040
Where are your thoughts at?

256
00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:54.560
I'm starting to feel like
my heart is not available anymore.

257
00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:02.800
It's been taken by a man,
who I recently met.

258
00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:07.680
Someone I've known for a while,

259
00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:10.360
but have learned to know again.

260
00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:13.040
What?

261
00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.560
You, Aksel.

262
00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:19.640
Hey...

263
00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:24.480
Why did we...?

264
00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:29.600
I mean, why did we...?

265
00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.440
Why did we get a divorce then?

266
00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.520
Well...

267
00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:41.640
We wouldn't have
gotten to know each other.

268
00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.200
You're right.

269
00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.320
Did you...

270
00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:58.400
Did you write that farewell letter?

271
00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.120
Yes, I have it.

272
00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:12.960
It's empty.

273
00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:16.160
This is also empty.

274
00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:18.680
Where's Shakespeare?

275
00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.120
Shakespeare?

276
00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:22.800
Shakespeare's...

277
00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:49.960
Oh my!
- What?

278
00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.400
Ave's home!

279
00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:52.560
So?

280
00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.080
This is our home, too.

281
00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:58.040
Yes, but we got divorced
a few hours ago.

282
00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.440
She can't find us like this.
It's schizophrenic.

283
00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.840
What will the kids think about this?
- This is not an affair.

284
00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.000
You think they'll be traumatized?

285
00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:10.360
We should talk about it
calmly and politely.

286
00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:14.280
This is not Brexit
that needs a referendum.

287
00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:15.840
Let's just tell them.

288
00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.320
We decided to try again.

289
00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:22.960
Yes, but let's tell them in the
morning in a responsible manner.

290
00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:25.880
Not get caught in bed
with our asses in the air.

291
00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:28.120
Yeah, you're right.

292
00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:40.560
It's quiet.

293
00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.200
She must've gone to her room.

294
00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:45.920
I'll try to sneak to
the living room couch.

295
00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:50.760
God, we're adults and doing this...

296
00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.160
In our own house, too.

297
00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.600
Mihkel!

298
00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.720
Well...

299
00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:11.800
Your dad and I decided
to stay together.

300
00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.800
So you didn't get divorced?

301
00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:19.400
No, we got an official divorce.

302
00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.920
And then decided to stay together?

303
00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:23.880
Yes.

304
00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.520
Are you going to get married now?

305
00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:31.240
That's something to consider, yes.

306
00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.680
Yeah, why not?

307
00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:38.240
Getting married is cheaper
than getting a divorce.

308
00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.600
Just the state fee.

309
00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:44.200
Are you honestly so bored that
you don't have anything better to do?

310
00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:48.640
Some midlifers go dancing
or play bridge.

311
00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:50.720
You decided to get a divorce.

312
00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.440
Guess so.

313
00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:56.240
Congratulations to all of us.

314
00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:58.240
Mihkel!
- Mihkel!

315
00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.640
Just joking.

316
00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.960
Thanks for the good wishes.

317
00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.800
Turns out Laura and I
are staying together.

318
00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:11.000
Oh my God!

319
00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:13.640
That's awesome, man!

320
00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.240
Unbelievable!

321
00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:17.440
We're having a wedding.

322
00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.440
You're going to be the best man.

323
00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:23.960
Shit, man!
Things will work out.

324
00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:27.800
I keep telling you that.
It'll work out for both you and me.

325
00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:31.760
If you and Mirjam happen to
have problems and need help,

326
00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:36.080
I know a therapist.
The one Mirjam told Laura about.

327
00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:40.600
I don't need a therapist,
I have my own therapy.

328
00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:44.720
I'm telling you,
this therapist is whack.

329
00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:48.120
His divorce therapy made
me and Laura reconcile.

330
00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.200
Get out of here!

331
00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:54.320
You should demand your money back.

332
00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:59.560
File an official complaint.

333
00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.760
Pitch the story for TV.

334
00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:09.800
Get an investigative journalist
to run a story on you.

335
00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.840
Hold on. Shush!

336
00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:16.400
Shush! Wait a second.

337
00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.560
Hello.

338
00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.200
Yeah, it's me.

339
00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:24.720
Yes?

340
00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:27.240
Reservist Tauno Karm here.

341
00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.240
Got it.
Over and out.

342
00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:30.760
What?

343
00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:32.080
Shit.

344
00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:36.760
Flash training for reservists 2019.

345
00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.400
I have to be there in 24 hours.

346
00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:39.640
Where's my uniform?

347
00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:42.000
Mirjam!
Shit, this is cool!

348
00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:45.840
This will kick off.
I got to go. You stay here.

349
00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:47.720
Mirjam!

350
00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.920
I told the realtor
that we're not selling.

351
00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:07.280
Rihard took a step back too,
so that's also fine.

352
00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.160
What?

353
00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:15.280
I got the job.
- What job?

354
00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.560
I'm going to be
making that film score.

355
00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:21.920
I knew I'd get it.
With ease.

356
00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:23.800
That's so cool.

357
00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:28.360
The bakery is also doing well
thanks to Mihkel's article.

358
00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:29.800
I can't manage the orders.

359
00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.440
We need to hire more people.

360
00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:36.680
In a strange way, we've really
benefited from the divorce.

361
00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:37.920
In every way.

362
00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.080
Yes, Mirjam?

363
00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.400
What training?

364
00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:46.320
Come here and let's talk.

365
00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:51.080
Those two.

366
00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:52.400
What?

367
00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:54.440
I think they're getting a divorce.

368
00:21:57.400 --> 00:22:00.640
As an experienced divorcee,
I saw it coming.

369
00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:10.520
Like this?

370
00:22:11.800 --> 00:22:12.880
Yeah.

371
00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:31.800
Oh my God,
this is so complicated.

372
00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:33.960
Well, what did you think?

373
00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:39.400
Playing the violin
is not like playing the zither.

374
00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:45.400
When's the right time to
start playing the violin? What age?

375
00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:47.200
It depends.

376
00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:49.440
Would be good to start
from the first grade.

377
00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:52.160
So, seven or eight.
- Yeah.

378
00:22:52.320 --> 00:22:54.240
What about 45?

379
00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:59.760
If you have the desire,
then there may be hope.

380
00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:02.760
How much do your lessons cost?

381
00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:07.080
With or without VAT?

382
00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:10.720
Those are your students.
- Yeah.

383
00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:14.440
I came to say that we have
one thing left to do.

384
00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:15.680
One thing?

385
00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:18.480
Yes, of course.

386
00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:20.960
Let's do it.

387
00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:33.280
The divorce agreement.

388
00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:35.840
Back to the universe.

389
00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:39.160
We need to come up with
a wedding plan.

390
00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:41.240
And the honeymoon.
- Yeah.

391
00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:44.440
We have to tell your parents.

392
00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:46.280
Oh my...

393
00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:50.200
Don't worry,
we'll explain it to them.

394
00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:54.680
In a nice way.
They deserve an explanation.

395
00:23:54.680 --> 00:23:55.800
Yeah, they do.

396
00:23:56.160 --> 00:24:00.120
'After all of that
you're going to stay together?'

397
00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:04.400
'Estonian men and
women should stay together.'

398
00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:06.480
What...

399
00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:08.960
Sorry.
That was your dad.

400
00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:14.320
They don't know half of
the things that went on here.

401
00:24:14.960 --> 00:24:15.960
God, yes.

402
00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:21.800
'How can they start
living together after all that?'

403
00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:29.280
'I guess there's therapy for that.'

404
00:24:43.400 --> 00:24:46.720
'Everything's squeaking.
Is there a man in the house?'

405
00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:49.040
Okay.

406
00:24:49.560 --> 00:24:50.800
Let's take it easy.

407
00:24:51.360 --> 00:24:56.920
Without any responsibilities,
parents, children...

408
00:24:57.120 --> 00:24:59.480
Without caring about
other people's opinions.

409
00:25:00.480 --> 00:25:01.480
Agreed?

410
00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:05.080
Mirjam and Tauno.

411
00:25:05.560 --> 00:25:07.120
Two Estonians.

412
00:25:07.720 --> 00:25:09.200
Just tell me.

413
00:25:09.520 --> 00:25:10.760
What's going on?

414
00:25:16.080 --> 00:25:18.680
You have to...
You're afraid...

415
00:25:19.160 --> 00:25:21.040
Sorry!

416
00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:24.240
Are you really asking that?
- Of course. How's it going?

417
00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:27.280
How's Holger? Is he...

418
00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:32.120
It's Ülo.

419
00:25:34.480 --> 00:25:37.720
You were talking about Holger.
Of course, Ülo.

420
00:25:37.840 --> 00:25:40.760
I had a brush next to the bed.

421
00:25:41.520 --> 00:25:43.240
To brush my hair in the morning.

422
00:25:44.120 --> 00:25:46.000
What a life...

423
00:25:48.200 --> 00:25:52.320
I wanted to stay
attractive for Laura.

424
00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:54.280
But now...

425
00:25:56.120 --> 00:25:58.560
I feel like I don't give a crap.

426
00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:01.280
All actors drink.

427
00:26:02.600 --> 00:26:04.720
DJs also drink.
- There you go.

428
00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:08.640
Laura's right.

429
00:26:09.840 --> 00:26:11.840
We were growing apart.

430
00:26:11.960 --> 00:26:14.440
I just can't...
Let's do it until the end.

431
00:26:14.480 --> 00:26:17.560
Maybe someone ate it.
Maybe it was the kids.

432
00:26:22.520 --> 00:26:24.560
We could have continued.

433
00:26:24.560 --> 00:26:26.400
Sorry.

434
00:26:26.480 --> 00:26:29.160
There was a time
when I'd go outside to burp.

435
00:26:29.160 --> 00:26:30.800
To avoid embarrassment.

436
00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:32.200
What kind of life is that?

437
00:26:32.240 --> 00:26:33.600
Let's take it from the top.

438
00:26:34.120 --> 00:26:35.480
This is sick.

439
00:26:35.680 --> 00:26:37.960
Sick how?
I even had a brush.

440
00:26:42.920 --> 00:26:45.520
God, there was a
time when I'd go outside...

441
00:26:47.720 --> 00:26:50.240
You don't know what
went on inside of him.

442
00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:53.600
He probably processed it
and pushed it down.

443
00:26:53.920 --> 00:26:55.760
And then acted like a knight.

444
00:26:56.360 --> 00:26:57.720
Aksel, too.

445
00:26:58.240 --> 00:26:59.600
He was so brave.

446
00:26:59.800 --> 00:27:02.280
Went and faced Tauno.

447
00:27:02.440 --> 00:27:04.840
Sometimes men are...

448
00:27:04.880 --> 00:27:07.800
Just thinking about it
makes the lights turn on.

449
00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:11.560
I'm just a castrated tomcat.

450
00:27:12.920 --> 00:27:15.280
Stop it or I'll smack your other eye.

451
00:27:15.280 --> 00:27:16.800
I'm sorry, Ago.

452
00:27:18.080 --> 00:27:19.960
Shit. Ago.

453
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:22.720
Just smack it.

454
00:27:22.760 --> 00:27:26.240
It's the second time today
that they've visited me

455
00:27:26.240 --> 00:27:28.920
and started accusing...

456
00:27:30.080 --> 00:27:31.960
Just smacking it.

457
00:27:34.640 --> 00:27:37.840
In spring, a ferret got in
through the window frame

458
00:27:37.880 --> 00:27:40.800
and peed everywhere.
It has an interesting aroma now.

459
00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:43.040
You should have a whiff.

460
00:27:43.080 --> 00:27:44.880
Aksel, damn it.

461
00:27:44.920 --> 00:27:46.640
Yes, honey?

462
00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:56.480
You value quality as well, I see?

463
00:27:58.480 --> 00:28:01.880
They took the confession quite...

464
00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:05.280
Done.

465
00:28:05.640 --> 00:28:10.720
What's this?
If the child looks like me, then...

466
00:28:11.400 --> 00:28:14.400
I have to have plastic surgery?
